                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9469100a-b6a9-313d-a09b-9852d6628e18",
                        "entry_id": "f42c985f-44b4-32a5-99cb-0bc24c1099bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. собирать растения для научно-исследовательских целей"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b77adfcf-3854-4fe4-a7bc-b2e8e3945ae0",
                                "sense_id": "9469100a-b6a9-313d-a09b-9852d6628e18",
                                "text": "На следующее утро Анна Сергеевна тотчас после завтрака отправилась ботанизировать с Базаровым и возвратилась перед самым обедом; Аркадий никуда не отлучался и провёл около часа с Катей."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f10853f4-a98f-4815-a262-7aae25b874d4",
                        "source_entry_id": "f42c985f-44b4-32a5-99cb-0bc24c1099bd",
                        "source_sense_id": "9469100a-b6a9-313d-a09b-9852d6628e18",
                        "target_lang_word": "botanise",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "botanise",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b51c4776-7e0a-395a-afda-a6260878a5a2",
                                        "entry_id": "7ce69b50-29b6-361b-a7ff-f3d7eb830469",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of botanize."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b6b252a-3714-4d8e-9f93-5031ffa73d99",
                                                "sense_id": "b51c4776-7e0a-395a-afda-a6260878a5a2",
                                                "text": "We were incompetent to map the country we passed through, to chart the waters, to geologise, botanise, zoologise, astronomise, or to any other ise."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73110ba1-36c3-4485-bee8-c11f3137965a",
                                                "sense_id": "b51c4776-7e0a-395a-afda-a6260878a5a2",
                                                "text": "This is a land of very great interest, even to those who do not specially botanise or 'zoologise.'"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8216b23-56a7-4b1b-b716-68c0a1ab3f66",
                                                "sense_id": "b51c4776-7e0a-395a-afda-a6260878a5a2",
                                                "text": "He sleeps by day because to be awake in sunlight would be, for him, an irresistible temptation to botanise, zoologise, nephelologise, and do no work."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a2a918b4-c542-40c1-a9ac-799ed5d60165",
                        "source_entry_id": "f42c985f-44b4-32a5-99cb-0bc24c1099bd",
                        "source_sense_id": "9469100a-b6a9-313d-a09b-9852d6628e18",
                        "target_lang_word": "botanize",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "botanize",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27f1b968-0b1b-3409-aac6-c867b0b77e08",
                                        "entry_id": "719b8ef8-5d0d-3ac0-a728-79241352b2f1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To do the work of a botanist, as to inventory the plant life in an area and to collect plants for research purposes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21f93d2a-5eb7-4867-9dd6-fd66c408212d",
                                                "sense_id": "27f1b968-0b1b-3409-aac6-c867b0b77e08",
                                                "text": "1770, Joseph Banks, The Endeavour Journal of Sir Joseph Banks, entry for 1770 January 22. http://gutenberg.net.au/plusfifty.html#banks\nDr Solander and Myself were botanizing"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e27f18d9-e688-4eac-af1b-7a24b605b257",
                                                "sense_id": "27f1b968-0b1b-3409-aac6-c867b0b77e08",
                                                "text": "When he was not studying, he was botanizing or mineralogizing with O'Toole's chaplain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97895f3d-c015-4b68-ba5c-aecf159b81c1",
                                                "sense_id": "27f1b968-0b1b-3409-aac6-c867b0b77e08",
                                                "text": "'Tis best when Frank takes his cousin ashore, / She loves botanising, / While Sissy who's left, can handle an oar / In a manner surprising."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "547785f3-8034-4e8f-8a5b-b75c3afeaf07",
                                                "sense_id": "27f1b968-0b1b-3409-aac6-c867b0b77e08",
                                                "text": "The only compensation he could get seems to have been to botanize and zoologize, as it were, on his visitors."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "408a898d-92fd-4bd9-9d86-5102f49afcdf",
                                                "sense_id": "27f1b968-0b1b-3409-aac6-c867b0b77e08",
                                                "text": "There it erects tents capable of holding about one hundred and fifty people, and there the members and their friends gather for a fortnight to climb mountains, botanize, zoologize, or merely enjoy life."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "40f5324b-3d59-480c-951c-e7bf8fe71f34",
                        "source_entry_id": "f42c985f-44b4-32a5-99cb-0bc24c1099bd",
                        "source_sense_id": "9469100a-b6a9-313d-a09b-9852d6628e18",
                        "target_lang_word": "botanizar",
